<article class="env-lemma" id="0DHP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DHP">Lemma <span data-tag="0DHP">85.36.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $U$ be a simplicial algebraic space over $S$. Let $a : U \to X$ be an augmentation. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. Let $\mathcal{F}_ n$ be the pullback to $U_{n, {\acute{e}tale}}$. If $U$ is a ph hypercovering of $X$, then there exists a canonical spectral sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(U_ p, \mathcal{F}_ p)  \]
</div>
  <p> converging to $H^{p + q}_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemmas <a href="/tag/0DHM" data-tag="0DHM">85.36.4</a> and <a href="/tag/09WJ" data-tag="09WJ">85.8.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>